{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And Zur.</b> The father of Cozbi. <b>The five kings of Midian.</b> It was necessary to write 'five,' to teach you that all five were equal in a single counsel for destruction against Israel. And Balaam went with them to take the wage of the counsel he had given, on account of which twenty-four thousand of Israel fell. And they would say to Israel: 'But when you were sixty myriads you did not have the strength to fight — how is it that you now come to fight against twelve thousand?'"], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:37:16.244526240Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}